FP3 -- GATE G-1, LINEAR COSMOLOGY WITH NO PRESCRIBED MASK, on the ungated C-H/K core: what, in the core's own
variables, can keep the MOND sector off in the linear web and on in galaxies -- and what no local mechanism can do.

WHY.  The ungated C-H/K core drives sigma_8 to 18-27 (L341, committed) and has no well-posed linearisation on its own
FRW (FP5, committed a26136bc4: at zero field U is pinned and the khronon's alpha_eff = alpha_c + 2 > 2).  Every repair
on the record is either posited (L359's vacuum gate, a prescribed mask) or, as a varied action term, unstable (a
threshold gate flat at both ends has W'' of both signs: DE7, DE12, DE13, CV3), blind (K-only: CV4) or leaks/slips
(curvature or matter readings: MS1, DE7).  This lane derives, from the core's own action: (i) why the core fails linear
cosmology; (ii) FP5's criterion and C1's stability rule for any local gate on the MOND energy; (iii) the most a stable
local gate can deliver (the chord bound) and one explicit construction at that bound; (iv) the construction proposed in
the G-1 brief (a leaf-average global factor times a convex local ramp), tested; (v) the resulting trilemma.

THE ACTION (the ungated core: astra's C-H, ACTION.md; L340's BPS terms with beta = 0; L350's leaf average; nu_mono):
    I = c^3/(16 pi G) Int d^4x sqrt(-g) { R - 2 Lambda + 2 h^{mn}(D_m U - a_m)(D_n U - a_n)
          + 2 alpha^2 q(h^{mn} D_m W_b D_n W_b / alpha^2) + Int_0^b dz L (d_z W - Delta_h W) + lambda_0 (W_0 - U)
          + alpha_c a_m a^m - c_2 (K - <K>_h)^2 } + GHY + S_m[g] + S_dark[g; declared cold state]
    alpha = a0/c^2;  q'(Z) = nu_mono(sqrt Z) - 1, q(0) = 0;  n_m = -d_m tau/sqrt(X), a_m = D_m ln N, K = nabla_m n^m.
    The dark mass is declared cold initial data at Omega_c (FP4 owns it).
THE GATES TESTED (one factor on the MOND term, 2 alpha^2 q -> 2 alpha^2 W q, varied with everything else):
    concave:  W = w(rho_dyn/rho_*(<K>_h)), w(u) = u/(1+u^4)^(1/4),  rho_dyn = (c^2/8 pi G)(<K>_h^2/3 - Lambda + 2 D_i a^i)
              (the dynamical density read off the clock's own acceleration divergence D_i a^i -- the physical
              potential's Laplacian -- plus the leaf mean); rho_* > 0 a function of the LEAF-AVERAGED expansion only.
    proposal: W = [Omega_L(<K>_h)/Omega_L0]^p ((x - x_c)_+ / (x_N - x_c))^n,  x = 4 pi G (rho_dyn - rho_bar)/H^2
              (proposed in the G-1 brief: a leaf-average global factor times a convex local ramp, flat only at the low end).
    threshold (control): a C^inf step flat at both ends (CV3's transition).
The footings: a0 = 9.3603e-11 (rho_Lambda) and 1.1312e-10 (rho_total), FP0.

  *** MUTATE=1: C4's concave gate is replaced by the threshold (flat-flat) gate with the same edge -- C4(c) and C4(d) must FAIL ***

================================================================================================================
A  THE CORE ON FRW: minisuperspace variation (sympy), leaf average vs plain c_2
================================================================================================================
  [PASS] A1 on FRW every C-H/K term but R - 2 Lambda vanishes (a_m = 0, U homogeneous, q(0) = 0, K = <K>), and the minisuperspace variation gives GR's Friedmann and acceleration equations: G_cos = G
         measured: H^2 = 8*pi*G*rho_0/(3*a(t)**3) + Lambda/3; a''/a = -4*pi*G*rho_0/(3*a(t)**3) + Lambda/3
  [PASS] A2 CONTROL: the plain -c_2 K^2 term (no leaf average) renormalises the Friedmann equation, H^2 (1 + 3 c_2/2) = 8 pi G rho/3 + Lambda/3 (L350's G_cos/G = 1/(1 + 3 c_2/2) at alpha_c = 0)
         measured: H^2 = 2*(8*pi*G*rho_0 + Lambda*a(t)**3)/(3*(3*c_2 + 2)*a(t)**3)
  [PASS] A3 a0 is absent from the background: the MOND term 2 alpha^2 q(0) = 0 and its first variation ~ (nu - 1) s -> 0 on FRW, so Friedmann is a0-blind; in the action a0 is a constant coupling: a0(z)/a0(0) = 1 on both footings
         measured: lim (nu-1)s = 0; a0 in the background equations: False; a0 = 9.3603e-11 / 1.1312e-10 m/s^2, a0(z)/a0(0) = 1 (canonical and alt)

================================================================================================================
B  WHY THE CORE FAILS LINEAR COSMOLOGY: the MOND energy is O(eps^(3/2)) around FRW
================================================================================================================
  [PASS] B1 ORDER COUNTING: q(Z) = (4/3) Z^(3/4) + ... ; with Z = |grad S U|^2/alpha^2 = O(eps^2) around FRW the core's MOND energy is O(eps^(3/2)), BELOW the O(eps^2) quadratic action, and its zero-field tangent q'(0) is infinite (FP5's pinned U); an AQUAL-type J(Y) ~ Y^(3/2) is O(eps^3) with zero tangent and drops out of linear order
         measured: q = -w**7/1260 + w**5/15 - w**4/2 + 4*w**3/3 (w = Z^(1/4)); leading Z exponent 3/4 (coef 4/3); eps order: core 3/2, AQUAL-type 3; zero-field tangent: core oo, AQUAL-type 0

================================================================================================================
B2-B3  THE YARDSTICK (L341's, re-implemented) AND THE UNGATED CORE
================================================================================================================
  [PASS] B2 CONTROL: the re-implemented yardstick reproduces L341's committed sigma_8 -- LCDM and the ungated core (canonical, c_2 = 0.0073, rms) -- to 1e-3; nu_mono = nu_RAR below the phantom peak (the kernel B1 expanded)
         measured: LCDM 0.81009 vs 0.81009; ungated 23.3139 vs 23.3139; |nu_mono/nu_RAR - 1| <= 4.9e-09
  [PASS] B3 THE UNGATED CORE FAILS G-1: at FP0's footings its MOND kernel on the linear web gives sigma_8 > 10 (both footings, rms and per-mode) -- the record's L341 failure, on this lane's inputs
         measured: canonical/rms 23.31, canonical/permode 17.71, alt/rms 27.55, alt/permode 20.84

================================================================================================================
C0  FP5'S WELL-POSEDNESS CRITERION, APPLIED TO A GATE (FP5's committed E(C), read and checked)
================================================================================================================
  [PASS] C0 FP5's committed reduced khronon E(C) (c_CH = 2) is E = alpha_c + 2C/(1+C): E(0) = alpha_c, E(inf) = alpha_c + 2, dE/dC > 0, and w^2 = c_2 (2 - E) k^2/(E (2 + 3 c_2)); with a gate the zero-field tangent is C_eff = W C_T, so the linearisation on FRW is well-posed iff C_eff < (2 - alpha_c)/alpha_c, and the MOND tangent vanishes IDENTICALLY on FRW iff W(FRW) = 0 with W = o(sqrt y) (C_T ~ y^(-1/2))
         measured: E = ((C_e + 1)*(alpha_c + 2) - 2)/(C_e + 1); E(0) = alpha_c; E(inf) = alpha_c + 2; dE/dC = 2/(C_e + 1)**2; E = 2 at C = [(2 - alpha_c)/alpha_c]; w^2 form check 0

================================================================================================================
C1  THE STABILITY RULE: a gate on the dynamical density is stable iff it is concave (sympy symbol)
================================================================================================================
  [PASS] C1 THE STABILITY RULE: B = 2 alpha^2 q >= 0 (q' = nu_mono - 1 >= 0, q(0) = 0); for a gate reading the lapse Laplacian the static symbol det = 16 k^6 [B W'' C^2 k^2 (1 + W C_T) - 4] has a zero at k^2 = 4/(B W'' C^2 (1+W C_T)) iff B W'' > 0; the gate's local term on matter is delta phi_loc = -pi G B W'' C^2 (1 + W C_T)^2 delta rho (an anti-pressure iff W'' > 0; CV3 G3/G4 in this reading); psi = phi (no slip).  STABLE <=> W CONCAVE
         measured: q >= 0 on the grid: True; det = 16*k2**3*(B*C**2*C_T*W2*Wbar*k2 + B*C**2*W2*k2 - 4); zero at k^2 = [4/(B*C**2*W2*(C_T*Wbar + 1))]; Newtonian part 4*pi*G*delta_rho*(-C_T*Wbar - 1)/k2; local part -pi*G*delta_rho*e*(C_T*Wbar + 1)**2 (k-independent: True); psi = phi: True; leaf-average lemma: delta<K> of a k != 0 mode = 0, so a factor F(<K>_h) adds 0 to the local second variation

