VERDICT
================================================================================================================
  The ungated core fails linear cosmology because its MOND energy is O(eps^(3/2)) around FRW with an infinite
  zero-field tangent (sigma_8 ~ 20; FP5's pinned U).  A local gate on the MOND energy is stable iff concave (C1),
  and a concave gate's on-fraction is capped by the density ratio (C3).  Spent at that bound, one concave gate built
  from the clock's D_i a^i and leaf average <K>_h keeps sigma_8 within 2% (D1 max 1.0000)
  with the flagship on for M_b <= 1e11 to z_on = 12.00, stable and unique -- but it cuts the L* outskirts, the
  1e12 flagship and KiDS, pushes 11-28% extra force into the z = 2.5-3 IGM, and is not zero on FRW (FP5's band
  shrinks to y < 0e+00 but survives).  Every gate that IS zero on FRW switches on from zero and is
  convex somewhere: the proposed convex ramp and the threshold carry C1's anti-pressure.  No local gate meets all
  three; the door left is a MOND term with a ZERO zero-field tangent on a field with its own inertia -- not in the core.
  Time 16 s.

